# Restrict the package by enumerating what to include (NFR-M-01).
# With the opposite approach of adding exclusions later, build outputs and working files
# added from then on would slip into the distributed package by default.
# When something new has to ship, add one line to this list to allow it explicitly.
**
!dist/extension.js
!dist/webview.js
!dist/webview.css
!icons/ahve-light.svg
!icons/ahve-dark.svg
!assets/icon.png
!package.json
!package.nls.json
!package.nls.*.json
!messages/**
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
# The authoring guide skill is allowed one file at a time. Allowing its directory would take in everything
# under it, so the distributed package would also carry the script's tests, which users never run.
!skills/agentic-html-visual-editor-authoring/SKILL.md
!skills/agentic-html-visual-editor-authoring/references/html-document.md
!skills/agentic-html-visual-editor-authoring/references/formatting.md
!skills/agentic-html-visual-editor-authoring/references/mermaid.md
!skills/agentic-html-visual-editor-authoring/references/comments.md
!skills/agentic-html-visual-editor-authoring/references/change-marks.md
!skills/agentic-html-visual-editor-authoring/scripts/list_comments.py
